  "notes": "{移|うつ}す means to move or transfer something from one place or state to another. It also has the distinct meaning of passing on an illness.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{移|うつ}る→移る：01232_utsuru⟧ (intransitive — to move, to shift)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{移|うつ}して⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates the action of moving/transferring is in progress.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{移|うつ}す: to move X to ~\n- ⟦{視線|しせん}→視線：14138_shisen⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{移|うつ}す: to shift one's gaze\n- ⟦{住|す}まい→住まい：11555_sumai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{移|うつ}す: to relocate one's home\n- ⟦{風邪|かぜ}→風邪：02188_kaze⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{移|うつ}す: to pass on a cold\n\nUSAGE:\nThe illness meaning (sense 2) uses the same kanji but is a separate usage. Be careful not to confuse with ⟦{写|うつ}す→写す：01227_utsusu⟧ (to copy, to photograph) or ⟦{映|うつ}す→映す：12963_utsusu⟧ (to reflect, to project).",
